# OrthoFlow — Code Owners & Review Domains
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# This file serves two purposes:
#
# 1. GitHub enforcement: `@parrish727` (the sole human account on this personal repo) is the
#    backstop owner. With the "Require review from Code Owners" ruleset option enabled on the
#    protected branches (main, production), this makes pktech_dev's approval required on any PR
#    into main/production — matching the branching model's human-escalation gate.
#
# 2. Agent review domains (source of truth): the delivery agents use the domain sections below
#    to know which changes they own for peer review on feature -> develop and develop -> main
#    PRs (agent-managed, per melanin-tech-global steering). Agents are not separate GitHub
#    accounts, so ownership resolves to @parrish727 in GitHub; the domain labels drive which
#    agent performs the review.
#
# Review domains:
#   DevOps   — CI/CD, infra, docker/compose, deploy scripts, nginx, k8s
#   Backend  — FastAPI routes/services/workers/models (with DBA on migrations/schema)
#   DBA      — Alembic migrations, DB models, queries, indexes
#   Frontend — React/Vite UI, and E2E (Playwright) tests
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Default owner — everything not matched below.
*                                   @parrish727

